   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "title": "Collision-risk models vs the naive forecast",
     "text": "On the ESA challenge test set (2,167 events, 150 high-risk) the naive forecast scores L = 0.694, matching the published value. The LightGBM gate scores 0.627 on the test set but 0.98 against 0.80 in cross-validation, and wins in 86% of bootstrap resamples. It is not reported as an improvement.",
